worktree: ../okay-wt-beside
spec: specs/intent-classify.md — a month with ANY number beside it is not a month named alone

why: `monthAlone` treated a neighbour as a day only when it was 1..31, so
  «с 12 по 40 сентября» (an impossible day, refused by the day parser on
  purpose) and «12-14 сентября» (a range, one token) both read as the whole
  of September. Found by okay-chat's TestWhen the moment its When.read
  asked the platform for periods. A month with a number beside it is
  somebody's date or range — never the bare month.
